   "body": "## Summary (macm3, 19:33 UTC)\n\n**Result.** Both M 40 circles are **unchanged** under the alias rule (main e82c7648, `hp/modecount_circle.py` of 14ddb64), and both \u03bb_phys circles wind +1.\n\n| D | circle (centre, R) | #231 | under the alias rule | verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 55.04 | 0.0612 + 3.8526 i, R 0.3 | winding 0 | winding **0** (29 points, largest step 0.382 rad, 0 mismatches, alias bisections 0, largest arc\u00b7scale 0.88) | unchanged |\n| 55.04 | \u03bb_phys 2.047684, R 0.2 (control) | +1, 2.047684 (4.6e-8) | **+1**, 2.047684 \u2212 0 i (4.6e-8), alias bisections 0 (0.52) | unchanged, control holds |\n| 61.03 | 2.0073 + 0.9727 i, R 0.2 | +1, zero 2.042590 + 1.150727 i (6.4e-3) | **+1**, zero **2.042590 + 1.150727 i** (6.4e-3), 37 points (30 before), largest step 0.352 rad, 0 mismatches, **alias bisections 9** (largest arc\u00b7scale 0.93) | unchanged (same zero, same estimate) |\n| 61.03 | \u03bb_phys 2.043533, R 0.2 (control) | +1, 2.043533 (2.1e-7) | **+1**, 2.043533 \u2212 0 i (2.1e-7), alias bisections 0 (0.49) | unchanged, control holds |\n\nSo the M 40 findings of #231 stand: the three M 48 zeros of D 55.04 are absent at M 40 (the U0 circle was one of them), and the D 61.03 row position 2.0073 + 0.9727 i holds a zero that has moved to 2.0426 + 1.1507 i.\n\n**New determinants.** Only the cached M 40 evals files were reused (copied from `I231-macm3`, evals only: 433 lines at D 55.04 and 856 at D 61.03, which hold #231's counts plus its circles); the alias rule added **1** new determinant at D 55.04 (433 \u2192 434) and **7** at D 61.03 (856 \u2192 863), 9 bisections of the D 61 circle's arcs. No winding and no position changed.\n\n**Run.** The commands of the issue with the same centres, radii and n0 20 as #231, `--M=40 --kf=23 --fmax=1e-15`, #231's tags, on the M 40 states of #231 loaded from `hp/data` (sha256 in the raw folder; setup |F| 3.3e-19 and 3.8e-19, no re-converge), 1 thread, nice 10, caffeinate -is, venv-macm3-314 (Python 3.14.3, python-flint 0.9.0, FLINT 3.6.0, `modecount_cx` with B = 5), exit 0 at 19:29:00 and 19:32:31 UTC, 28 s and 210 s, awake. `hp/data` is clean for this run (the states are back in the raw folder).\n\n**Acceptance.** Each winding is unchanged (none corrected), the \u03bb_phys control at each D winds +1.\n\n**Discrepancies.** None.\n\n**Raw.** `I269-macm3/` of the raw-data repository, commit 1656d42 (the two circle logs, the copied caches, the states' sha256, exits.txt, awake.py and .log, README). `raw_check.py` exits 0.\n\n### Recommended tasks\n\nNone.\n",
